# Local extensions to the OAIS Information Model schema (oais_im_schema-sh-v5.ttl),
# in the same im: namespace, loaded alongside it.
#
# Two kinds of thing are kept here rather than in the generated schema:
#   - groups of Representation Information, format profiles, the terms for
#     naming descriptions and view specifications as files, where an
#     object's bits are stored, and the semantics of data elements (units,
#     scaling, fill values, valid ranges, code lists), new here and marked
#     oais:status "local-extension". Some were in the RiC bridge
#     (bridge:hasStorageLocation, bridge:structuralPath, ...) or RiC-O
#     itself (rico:hasUnitOfMeasurement, rico:UnitOfMeasurement) until
#     moved here, so that nothing here depends on RiC-O or the bridge to it;
#     the archive renames the old terms in its data at startup;
#   - Designated Community, Preservation Objective and Transformation
#     Information Property, with the properties that relate them, moved here
#     from the generated schema, keeping their identifiers but now marked
#     oais:status "local-extension"; and Agent, who defines or identifies
#     them, moved here too, already a local extension there.
# The knowledge base the schema is generated from, and its workflow, need the
# same changes, or regenerating the schema will bring the moved classes back.

@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix im: <http://ontology.oais.info/im/> .
@prefix oais: <http://ontology.oais.info/meta/> .

# ---- Groups of Representation Information ----
#
# OAIS does not say so explicitly, but a Data Object often needs several
# pieces of Representation Information used together (its Structure AND its
# Semantic Representation Information), and there are often alternatives any
# one of which will do (a DFDL OR a Kaitai Struct description of the same
# structure; Microsoft Excel OR any application that reads OOXML
# spreadsheets). Groups nest: an alternative can itself be an AND group, e.g.
# a DFDL schema AND a DFDL processor to apply it.
#
# A group is itself Representation Information, so it can stand wherever
# Representation Information can -- including as the object of
# im:hasStructureRepresentationInformation, im:hasSemanticRepresentationInformation
# or im:hasOtherRepresentationInformation, whose cardinality of one each is
# unaffected: an OR group of structure descriptions is one Structure
# Representation Information. The groups sit alongside those properties
# rather than replacing them. Group members are unordered.

im:RepInfoGroup
  a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Representation Information Group" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:subClassOf im:RepresentationInformation ;
  rdfs:comment "Representation Information Group: Representation Information made up of other Representation Information, its members (im:hasGroupMember), each of which may itself be a group. A group that is neither an AND group nor an OR group is taken to be an AND group. A group may also be typed with the category of Representation Information it provides (Structure, Semantic or Other). LOCAL EXTENSION -- OAIS does not define groups of Representation Information; see also info.oais.infomodel.interfaces.representationinformation.RepInfoGroup in oaisCore." .

im:RepInfoAndGroup
  a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Representation Information AND Group" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:subClassOf im:RepInfoGroup ;
  rdfs:comment "Representation Information AND Group: a group all of whose members must be used together, e.g. the Structure Representation Information and the Semantic Representation Information of a Data Object, or a structure description and the software that applies it. Its members may be of different categories. LOCAL EXTENSION -- see im:RepInfoGroup." .

im:RepInfoOrGroup
  a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Representation Information OR Group" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:subClassOf im:RepInfoGroup ;
  rdfs:comment "Representation Information OR Group: a group whose members are equivalent alternatives, any one of which is enough, e.g. DFDL, Kaitai Struct and DRB descriptions of the same structure, or Microsoft Excel and any application that reads OOXML spreadsheets. The members provide the same category of Representation Information, with which the group may also be typed. Being members of the same OR group asserts their equivalence; like any Information Object, a member may also carry Provenance Information testifying to it. LOCAL EXTENSION -- see im:RepInfoGroup." .

im:hasGroupMember
  a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "has Group Member" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:RepInfoGroup ;
  rdfs:range im:RepresentationInformation ;
  rdfs:comment "Links a Representation Information Group to one of its members. Members are unordered. LOCAL EXTENSION -- see im:RepInfoGroup." .

# ---- Format profiles ----
#
# A format registry identifier such as a PRONOM PUID is generally not enough
# to read a file: PRONOM's x-fmt/111 (plain text) says nothing about the
# character encoding, x-fmt/18 (CSV) nothing about the delimiter, and a
# spreadsheet format has versions and conformance classes. A format profile
# refines a registry identifier with what it leaves out.

im:FormatProfile
  a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Format Profile" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:subClassOf im:StructureRepresentationInformation ;
  rdfs:comment "Format Profile: Structure Representation Information identifying a Data Object's format precisely -- a format registry identifier (e.g. a PRONOM PUID), refined with what the identifier leaves out: the version or conformance class of the specification, the character encoding, line endings, field delimiter and quote character, and the media type -- and pointing to the specification (rdfs:seeAlso). LOCAL EXTENSION -- OAIS does not define it." .

im:formatRegistryIdentifier
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:label "format registry identifier" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:FormatProfile ;
  rdfs:comment "The format's identifier in a format registry, prefixed by the registry, e.g. 'PRONOM fmt/214'. LOCAL EXTENSION -- see im:FormatProfile." .

im:formatVersion
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:label "format version" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:FormatProfile ;
  rdfs:comment "The version or conformance class of the format's specification, e.g. 'ECMA-376 Transitional'. LOCAL EXTENSION -- see im:FormatProfile." .

im:mediaType
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:label "media type" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:FormatProfile ;
  rdfs:comment "The format's IANA media type, e.g. 'text/csv'. LOCAL EXTENSION -- see im:FormatProfile." .

im:characterEncoding
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:label "character encoding" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:FormatProfile ;
  rdfs:comment "The character encoding of a text format, by its IANA charset name, e.g. 'UTF-8'. LOCAL EXTENSION -- see im:FormatProfile." .

im:lineEnding
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:label "line ending" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:FormatProfile ;
  rdfs:comment "How lines end in a text format: 'CRLF', 'LF' or 'CR'. LOCAL EXTENSION -- see im:FormatProfile." .

im:fieldDelimiter
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:label "field delimiter" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:FormatProfile ;
  rdfs:comment "The character separating fields in delimited text, e.g. ',' or 'TAB'. LOCAL EXTENSION -- see im:FormatProfile." .

im:quoteCharacter
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:label "quote character" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:FormatProfile ;
  rdfs:comment "The character enclosing fields that contain the delimiter in delimited text, e.g. '\"'. LOCAL EXTENSION -- see im:FormatProfile." .

# ---- Descriptions and view specifications as files ----
#
# What a Representation Information manifest needs to name each description
# explicitly (see oais-structure-manifest): where a file is
# (im:hasStorageLocation, also where a Data Object's own bits are), which
# language a structure description is in, its text, the class generated from
# it where that's how it's applied, and view specifications -- how to view
# decoded data as a table, image, time series or vector.

im:hasStorageLocation
  a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "has storage location" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:subPropertyOf rdfs:seeAlso ;
  rdfs:comment "Points to the actual retrievable location of an object's bits (e.g. a Dropbox link, cloud storage URI) -- more specific and self-documenting than plain rdfs:seeAlso for this one purpose. Used on an im:DataObject/im:DigitalObject and on a description or view specification given as a file, so it has no declared domain. LOCAL EXTENSION -- OAIS treats where bits are kept, and how they are retrieved, as implementation-specific and out of scope for the reference model." .

im:specificationLanguage
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:label "specification language" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:RepresentationInformation ;
  rdfs:comment "The language a machine-readable description is written in, so software knows how to apply it: 'DFDL', 'Kaitai Struct', 'DRB SDF', 'DRB' (no description: DRB recognises the format itself) or 'drb-python' (a driver package). LOCAL EXTENSION." .

im:specificationText
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:label "specification text" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:RepresentationInformation ;
  rdfs:comment "The full text of a machine-readable description or view specification held in the archive, e.g. a DFDL schema; the archive serves it as a file. LOCAL EXTENSION." .

im:generatedClassName
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:label "generated class name" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:StructureRepresentationInformation ;
  rdfs:comment "For a description applied through code generated from it (a Kaitai Struct .ksy): the fully qualified name of the generated class. LOCAL EXTENSION." .

im:ViewSpecification
  a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "View Specification" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:subClassOf im:SemanticRepresentationInformation ;
  rdfs:comment "View Specification: Semantic Representation Information saying how to view decoded data -- as a table (which elements are rows, which columns, with their units and meanings), a time series or a vector -- for tools such as TOPCAT and SPLAT. LOCAL EXTENSION." .

im:viewKind
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:label "view kind" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:ViewSpecification ;
  rdfs:comment "What a view specification shows the data as: 'table', 'image', 'timeSeries' or 'vector'. LOCAL EXTENSION." .

# ---- Semantics of data elements ----
#
# Used by RepInfo Tools when it saves a format description: every element of
# the description (a field, record, choice or choice branch) gets its own
# im:SemanticRepresentationInformation, nested to mirror the description via
# im:interpretedUsingRecurse, with rdfs:label (the semantic name),
# skos:definition and the properties below: where the element sits in the
# structure, its units, how raw values become physical ones, which values
# mean "no data", the valid range, coded values, and links to controlled
# vocabularies. Names follow the CF metadata conventions (scale_factor,
# add_offset, _FillValue, valid_min, valid_max) that scientific data already
# uses.

im:structuralPath
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:label "structural path" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:SemanticRepresentationInformation ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:comment "Which element of a format description a Semantic Representation Information is about, as its dotted path from the top of the file (e.g. packet.body.science.temp) -- the link between what a value means and where it sits in the bytes. LOCAL EXTENSION." .

im:UnitOfMeasurement
  a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Unit of Measurement" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:comment "Unit of Measurement: a unit in which the values of a data element are expressed, e.g. 'K' or 'erg/cm2/s/Angstrom', named by its rdfs:label and, where known, matched to a term in a units vocabulary with skos:exactMatch. LOCAL EXTENSION -- OAIS leaves the content of Semantic Representation Information to the Archive." .

im:hasUnitOfMeasurement
  a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "has unit of measurement" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:SemanticRepresentationInformation ;
  rdfs:range im:UnitOfMeasurement ;
  rdfs:comment "The unit in which a data element's physical values are expressed. LOCAL EXTENSION." .

im:scaleFactor
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:label "scale factor" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:SemanticRepresentationInformation ;
  rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment "Physical value = raw value * scale factor + add offset (CF convention scale_factor; FITS BSCALE). LOCAL EXTENSION." .

im:addOffset
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:label "add offset" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:SemanticRepresentationInformation ;
  rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment "See im:scaleFactor (CF convention add_offset; FITS BZERO). LOCAL EXTENSION." .

im:fillValue
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:label "fill value" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:SemanticRepresentationInformation ;
  rdfs:comment "The raw value that means 'no data' for this element (CF convention _FillValue). LOCAL EXTENSION." .

im:validMin
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:label "smallest valid value" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:SemanticRepresentationInformation ;
  rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment "The smallest meaningful physical value of this element (CF convention valid_min). LOCAL EXTENSION." .

im:validMax
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:label "largest valid value" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:SemanticRepresentationInformation ;
  rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:comment "The largest meaningful physical value of this element (CF convention valid_max). LOCAL EXTENSION." .

im:hasCodeList
  a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "has code list" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:SemanticRepresentationInformation ;
  rdfs:range skos:ConceptScheme ;
  rdfs:comment "For a coded element: the skos:ConceptScheme of its codes, each a skos:Concept whose skos:notation is the raw value and skos:prefLabel its meaning. LOCAL EXTENSION." .

im:representsConcept
  a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "represents concept" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:subPropertyOf rdfs:seeAlso ;
  rdfs:domain im:SemanticRepresentationInformation ;
  rdfs:comment "The concept, in an external vocabulary or ontology, that this element's values represent. LOCAL EXTENSION." .

# ---- Transformations ----
#
# OAIS names three ways of preserving digital information: adding
# Representation Information, Transformation (a Digital Migration that changes
# the Content Information or PDI, checked against Transformation Information
# Properties, with Provenance Information added), and handing complete AIPs to
# another archive. The Information Model has classes for the second's result
# but not for the Transformation itself, so these record one: what it started
# from and made, how (the mapping it followed), when, and how each
# Transformation Information Property fared. The new Data Object goes in an
# AIP Version, whose Provenance Information records the Transformation.

im:Transformation
  a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Transformation" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:comment "Transformation: a Digital Migration in which the Content Information or Preservation Description Information of an Archival Information Package is changed, e.g. its Data Object rewritten in another format. Records the Data Object it started from (im:transformationSource), the one it made (im:transformationResult), the mapping it followed (im:followedMapping), when (im:performedAt), and its checks of Transformation Information Properties (im:hasPropertyCheck). LOCAL EXTENSION -- OAIS defines Transformation but the Information Model has no class for one." .

im:NonReversibleTransformation
  a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Non-Reversible Transformation" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:subClassOf im:Transformation ;
  rdfs:comment "Non-Reversible Transformation: a Transformation that can't be shown to be reversible, e.g. because some values weren't carried over, or were scaled or rounded. Checks of Transformation Information Properties are the evidence that what matters was kept. LOCAL EXTENSION." .

im:transformationSource
  a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "transformation source" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:Transformation ;
  rdfs:range im:DataObject ;
  rdfs:comment "The Data Object a Transformation started from, which it leaves unchanged. LOCAL EXTENSION." .

im:transformationResult
  a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "transformation result" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:Transformation ;
  rdfs:range im:DataObject ;
  rdfs:comment "The Data Object a Transformation made. LOCAL EXTENSION." .

im:performedAt
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:label "performed at" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:Transformation ;
  rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
  rdfs:comment "When a Transformation was done. LOCAL EXTENSION." .

im:TransformationMapping
  a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Transformation Mapping" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:comment "Transformation Mapping: how a Transformation made each element of the new format from the old, one rule per line in im:specificationText (im:specificationLanguage 'OAIS Transformation Mapping'), e.g. 'star.ra = stars.entry.ra * 0.0174532925'. Kept so the Transformation can be understood and repeated. LOCAL EXTENSION." .

im:followedMapping
  a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "followed mapping" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:Transformation ;
  rdfs:range im:TransformationMapping ;
  rdfs:comment "The mapping a Transformation followed. LOCAL EXTENSION." .

im:TransformationInformationPropertyCheck
  a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Transformation Information Property Check" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:comment "Transformation Information Property Check: whether one Transformation Information Property's values were preserved by a Transformation (im:checkOutcome: 'preserved', 'changed' or 'not checked'), found by decoding the new Data Object with its own Representation Information and comparing physical values, with the details in rdfs:comment. LOCAL EXTENSION -- OAIS says such checks may be part of Provenance Information." .

im:hasPropertyCheck
  a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "has property check" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:Transformation ;
  rdfs:range im:TransformationInformationPropertyCheck ;
  rdfs:comment "A check of a Transformation Information Property made for a Transformation. LOCAL EXTENSION." .

im:checksProperty
  a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "checks property" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:TransformationInformationPropertyCheck ;
  rdfs:range im:TransformationInformationProperty ;
  rdfs:comment "The Transformation Information Property a check is of. LOCAL EXTENSION." .

im:checkOutcome
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:label "check outcome" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:TransformationInformationPropertyCheck ;
  rdfs:comment "Whether the property's values were 'preserved', 'changed', or 'not checked' (e.g. because the units differ). LOCAL EXTENSION." .

im:sourcePath
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:label "source path" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:TransformationInformationPropertyCheck ;
  rdfs:comment "Where the checked values are in the old format, as an im:structuralPath. LOCAL EXTENSION." .

im:targetPath
  a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:label "target path" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:TransformationInformationPropertyCheck ;
  rdfs:comment "Where the checked values went in the new format, as an im:structuralPath. LOCAL EXTENSION." .

im:AIPVersion
  a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "AIP Version" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:subClassOf im:ArchivalInformationPackage ;
  rdfs:comment "AIP Version: an AIP whose Content Information or Preservation Description Information has undergone a Transformation on a source AIP (im:hasSourceAIP, where there is one), and is a candidate to replace it. LOCAL EXTENSION -- an OAIS term the Information Model has no class for." .

im:hasSourceAIP
  a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "has source AIP" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:AIPVersion ;
  rdfs:range im:ArchivalInformationPackage ;
  rdfs:comment "The AIP an AIP Version was made from by a Transformation. LOCAL EXTENSION." .

im:recordsTransformation
  a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "records transformation" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  rdfs:domain im:ProvenanceInformation ;
  rdfs:range im:Transformation ;
  rdfs:comment "A Transformation that Provenance Information records. LOCAL EXTENSION." .

# ---- Designated Community, Preservation Objectives and Transformation ----
# ---- Information Properties, and the Agent who defines or identifies  ----
# ---- them (moved from oais_im_schema-sh-v5.ttl)                        ----

@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://ontology.oais.info/im/Agent>
  a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Agent" ;
  oais:identifier "c-0029" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  oais:edition "CCSDS 650.0-M-3 (Issue 3, December 2024)" ;
  rdfs:comment "Agent: A person, organization, or automated system capable of performing an action such as defining a Designated Community or Preservation Objective, or identifying a Transformation Information Property. LOCAL EXTENSION -- the OAIS Information Model does not itself model who performs such actions; that belongs to the Producer/Management/Consumer roles of the Functional Model, out of scope for the Information-Model-only schema." .

<http://ontology.oais.info/im/DesignatedCommunity>
  a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Designated Community" ;
  oais:identifier "c-0026" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  oais:edition "CCSDS 650.0-M-3 (Issue 3, December 2024)" ;
  oais:oaisConcept "Designated Community" ;
  oais:sourceReference "glossary" ;
  oais:sourceReference "section 2.4" ;
  rdfs:comment "Designated Community: An identified group of potential Consumers who should be able to understand a particular set of information in ways exemplified by the Preservation Objectives. The Designated Community may be composed of multiple user communities. A Designated Community is defined by the Archive and this definition may change over time. Not diagrammed as a class in the OAIS figures." .

<http://ontology.oais.info/im/PreservationObjective>
  a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Preservation Objective" ;
  oais:identifier "c-0027" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  oais:edition "CCSDS 650.0-M-3 (Issue 3, December 2024)" ;
  oais:oaisConcept "Preservation Objective" ;
  oais:sourceReference "section 2.4" ;
  rdfs:comment "Preservation Objective: A specific achievable aim which can be carried out using the Information Object. Per section 2.4, an OAIS must define its Preservation Objectives, which should be Specific, Actionable, and Measurable, and which exemplify what it means for information to be Independently Understandable by the Designated Community." .

<http://ontology.oais.info/im/TransformationInformationProperty>
  a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Transformation Information Property" ;
  skos:altLabel "Transformational Information Property" ;
  oais:identifier "c-0028" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  oais:edition "CCSDS 650.0-M-3 (Issue 3, December 2024)" ;
  oais:oaisConcept "Transformation Information Property" ;
  oais:sourceReference "glossary" ;
  oais:sourceReference "section 2.5" ;
  rdfs:subClassOf [
    a owl:Restriction ;
    owl:onProperty <http://ontology.oais.info/im/dependsOnRepresentationInformation> ;
    owl:minCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger
  ] ;
  rdfs:comment "Transformation Information Property: An Information Property the preservation of the value of which is regarded as being necessary but not sufficient to verify that any Non-Reversible Transformation has adequately preserved information content. This could be important as contributing to evidence about Authenticity. Such an Information Property is dependent upon specific Representation Information, including Semantic Representation Information, to denote how it is encoded and what it means. NOTE -- sometimes referred to in the literature as a 'significant property'. Per section 2.5, checks of the values of Transformation Information Properties may be part of Provenance Information; not asserted here as a formal relation since OAIS states it as a possibility, not a requirement." .

<http://ontology.oais.info/im/carriedOutUsing>
  a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "carried out using" ;
  oais:identifier "s-0036" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  oais:slotRole "mapped" ;
  rdfs:domain <http://ontology.oais.info/im/PreservationObjective> ;
  rdfs:range <http://ontology.oais.info/im/InformationObject> ;
  rdfs:comment "sources:section 2.4 ('A specific achievable aim which can be carried out using the Information Object')." .

<http://ontology.oais.info/im/definesPreservationObjective>
  a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "defines Preservation Objective" ;
  oais:identifier "s-0037" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  oais:slotRole "mapped" ;
  rdfs:domain <http://ontology.oais.info/im/Agent> ;
  rdfs:range <http://ontology.oais.info/im/PreservationObjective> ;
  rdfs:comment "sources:section 2.4 ('An OAIS must define Preservation Objectives'). Domain is Agent, not OAIS: it is a person, organization, or automated system acting on the Archive's behalf that performs the defining, not the Archive-as-system itself." .

<http://ontology.oais.info/im/dependsOnRepresentationInformation>
  a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "depends on Representation Information" ;
  oais:identifier "s-0038" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  oais:slotRole "mapped" ;
  rdfs:domain <http://ontology.oais.info/im/TransformationInformationProperty> ;
  rdfs:range <http://ontology.oais.info/im/RepresentationInformation> ;
  rdfs:comment "sources:glossary ('Such an Information Property is dependent upon specific Representation Information, including Semantic Representation Information, to denote how it is encoded and what it means')." .

<http://ontology.oais.info/im/hasDesignatedCommunity>
  a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "has Designated Community" ;
  oais:identifier "s-0042" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  oais:slotRole "mapped" ;
  rdfs:domain <http://ontology.oais.info/im/InformationObject> ;
  rdfs:range <http://ontology.oais.info/im/DesignatedCommunity> ;
  rdfs:comment "sources:glossary. Relates a specific Information Object -- including an Information Package, since InformationPackage is a subclass of InformationObject, so this also covers a collection such as an AIP or DIP -- to the Designated Community(ies) for which it must be Independently Understandable. Distinct from definesDesignatedCommunity, which is the Archive's own archive-wide definition; an object may be relevant to several Designated Communities, so no cardinality restriction is asserted." .

<http://ontology.oais.info/im/definesDesignatedCommunity>
  a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "defines Designated Community" ;
  oais:identifier "s-0039" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  oais:slotRole "mapped" ;
  rdfs:domain <http://ontology.oais.info/im/Agent> ;
  rdfs:range <http://ontology.oais.info/im/DesignatedCommunity> ;
  rdfs:comment "sources:glossary ('A Designated Community is defined by the Archive and this definition may change over time'). Domain is Agent, not OAIS: it is a person, organization, or automated system acting on the Archive's behalf that performs the defining, not the Archive-as-system itself." .

<http://ontology.oais.info/im/hasPreservationObjective>
  a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "has Preservation Objective" ;
  oais:identifier "s-0040" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  oais:slotRole "mapped" ;
  rdfs:domain <http://ontology.oais.info/im/DesignatedCommunity> ;
  rdfs:range <http://ontology.oais.info/im/PreservationObjective> ;
  rdfs:comment "sources:glossary ('...should be able to understand a particular set of information in ways exemplified by the Preservation Objectives')." .

<http://ontology.oais.info/im/hasTransformationInformationProperty>
  a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "has Transformation Information Property" ;
  oais:identifier "s-0043" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  oais:slotRole "mapped" ;
  rdfs:domain <http://ontology.oais.info/im/InformationObject> ;
  rdfs:range <http://ontology.oais.info/im/TransformationInformationProperty> ;
  rdfs:comment "sources:glossary; section 2.5. Relates a specific Information Object -- including an Information Package, since InformationPackage is a subclass of InformationObject, so this also covers a collection such as an AIP or DIP -- to the Transformation Information Property value(s) that must be checked to evidence adequate preservation of its content across a Non-Reversible Transformation. Distinct from identifiesTransformationInformationProperty, which is the Archive's own archive-wide designation; no cardinality restriction is asserted, since an object may have several." .

<http://ontology.oais.info/im/identifiesTransformationInformationProperty>
  a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "identifies Transformation Information Property" ;
  oais:identifier "s-0041" ;
  oais:status "local-extension" ;
  oais:slotRole "mapped" ;
  rdfs:domain <http://ontology.oais.info/im/Agent> ;
  rdfs:range <http://ontology.oais.info/im/TransformationInformationProperty> ;
  rdfs:comment "sources:section 2.5 ('the following should also be preserved: Definition of the Designated Communities; Preservation Objectives; Transformational Information Properties'). Domain is Agent, not OAIS: it is a person, organization, or automated system acting on the Archive's behalf that performs the identifying, not the Archive-as-system itself." .
